diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 5acf1d8..4f9bd14 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -1 +1,29 @@
 # jobq — a small persistent job queue with a command-line front-end
+
+An OTP application: a supervised `Jobq.Queue` GenServer holds the queue, `Jobq.Core` has the
+queue rules, `Jobq.Store` persists the state file and `Jobq.CLI` is the escript front-end.
+
+## Build and test
+
+```
+mix escript.build     # produces ./jobq
+mix test
+mix format --check-formatted
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+```
+jobq add NAME [--payload TEXT] [--priority 0-9] [--delay S | --at T] [--max-attempts N] [--backoff S]
+jobq take [--lease S]          # prints <id>\t<name>\t<payload>
+jobq ack ID | fail ID [--error TEXT] | retry ID | cancel ID
+jobq list [--state ready|scheduled|running|done|dead]
+jobq show ID | stats | purge
+```
+
+`JOBQ_STATE` selects the state file (default `jobq.state`); `JOBQ_NOW` overrides the clock
+(Unix seconds). Failed jobs are retried after `backoff * 2^(attempts-1)` seconds (at most an
+hour) until `max_attempts` is reached, then they are dead until `retry`.
+
+Exit codes: 0 ok, 1 unknown job, 2 usage error, 3 state file error, 4 no job ready,
+5 job in the wrong state.
